Description: CVE-2026-56000 - glx: free old context tag before allocating new one in CommonMakeCurrent
 Use-after-free in the GLX server extension. In CommonMakeCurrent() the local
 variable oldTag is a pointer into cl->contextTags[]. CommonMakeNewCurrent()
 may call GlxAllocContextTag() which can realloc() cl->contextTags, moving the
 array and leaving oldTag as a dangling pointer. A subsequent
 GlxFreeContextTag(oldTag) then writes into freed memory, resulting in a
 use-after-free reachable by any local X client (CWE-416, CVSS 7.8).
 .
 The fix ensures GlxFreeContextTag(oldTag) is invoked - and oldTag
 immediately nulled - BEFORE CommonMakeNewCurrent() is called, so no
 dangling pointer into the tag array can survive across a potential realloc.
 .
 Backport note for xorg-server 21.1.7 (Debian bookworm):
 The vulnerable trailing GlxFreeContextTag(oldTag) call that the upstream
 commit removed was introduced by upstream refactor 4781f2a5a8c2 ("GLX:
 Free the tag of the old context later"), which is NOT present in this
 branch. In 21.1.7 CommonLoseCurrent() already frees the tag internally on
 success, and CommonMakeCurrent() nulls oldTag right after. This backport
 therefore adds only the explicit GlxFreeContextTag(oldTag) call before
 the existing oldTag = NULL assignment: it matches upstream's fix pattern,
 makes the free explicit at the call site, and provides defence in depth
 against any future refactor that removes the internal free from
 CommonLoseCurrent().
 .
 The upstream test files (test/pyxtest/proto/glx.py, test/pyxtest/test_glx.py)
 are omitted from this backport: they depend on the pyxtest harness which
 does not exist in xorg-server 21.1.7.
 .
 Introduced-by: 4781f2a5a8c2 ("GLX: Free the tag of the old context later")
 Reported-by: Anonymous working with Trend Micro Zero Day Initiative
Origin: backport, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/xserver/-/commit/2779affbdb4354e894f490e56f962527d6125043
Bug: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/xserver/-/merge_requests/2250
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1141703
Author: Peter Hutterer <peter.hutterer@who-t.net>
Last-Update: 2026-07-12

--- a/glx/vndcmds.c
+++ b/glx/vndcmds.c
@@ -259,6 +259,10 @@
             if (ret != Success) {
                 return ret;
             }
+            // Free the old tag before calling CommonMakeNewCurrent(),
+            // which may call GlxAllocContextTag() and realloc the
+            // contextTags array, invalidating the oldTag pointer.
+            GlxFreeContextTag(oldTag);
             oldTag = NULL;
         }
 
