Description: Fix CVE-2026-55999 heap-buffer-overflow via PCF fonts with malicious per-glyph metrics
 A crafted PCF font can present per-glyph metrics that violate the font's
 maxbounds invariant (or that are negative). glamor_font_get() sizes its
 texture atlas slots from maxbounds but copies each glyph using
 GLYPHHEIGHTPIXELS/GLYPHWIDTHBYTES from the per-glyph data, producing an
 out-of-bounds heap write with attacker-controlled extent and content.
 .
 This backport combines two upstream commits:
   * fbf7bac22e2c6bd627fb042742a23318263edae1
     "glamor: reject fonts with per-glyph metrics exceeding maxbounds"
     - Reject fonts where the maxbounds-derived slot size is <= 0.
     - Reject any glyph whose per-glyph metrics are negative or exceed
       the atlas slot size, freeing the texture/atlas and returning NULL
       so glamor falls back to software rendering.
     - Switch the memcpy loop to use the validated width/height values.
   * e31efd3e106e53bfc29d499ff0a34b0d20013f2d
     "fb/mi/glamor: reject glyphs with negative dimensions"
     - Tighten the `if (w && h)` gates in fb/glamor/mi poly_glyph_blt
       paths to `if (w > 0 && h > 0)` so signed negative dimensions are
       also rejected.
 .
 The upstream in-patch tests live under test/pyxtest/ which does not
 exist in xorg-server 21.1.7; those hunks are omitted from this backport.
